Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Clock Synchronization
Kerberos requires synchronized clocks. If authentication fails:

# Check system time
date

# Synchronize with NTP (if available)
ntpdate -s time.nist.gov

# Or manually set time
timedatectl set-time "2023-12-01 10:00:00"
Issue 2: DNS Resolution Problems
Ensure proper hostname resolution:

# Test DNS resolution
nslookup kdc-server.example.com

# Check hosts file
cat /etc/hosts

# Test connectivity
ping kdc-server.example.com
Issue 3: Firewall Blocking
Check firewall settings:

# Check firewall status
firewall-cmd --list-all

# Test port connectivity
telnet kdc-server.example.com 88
Issue 4: Permission Problems
Check file permissions:

# Check krb5.conf permissions
ls -la /etc/krb5.conf

# Check ticket cache permissions
ls -la /tmp/krb5cc_*
Security Best Practices
Secure Configuration Guidelines
Use Strong Encryption: Ensure AES encryption is enabled
Regular Password Changes: Implement password rotation policies
Ticket Lifetime Management: Configure appropriate ticket lifetimes
Secure Key Storage: Protect keytab files with proper permissions
Network Security: Use encrypted connections where possible
